From d442631e99ab522c79b8976521a209e9f77150c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DSF PC Port <jmokikearns@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:02:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] Video timing: the hardware's frame periods, by standard
 and interlace

The VBlank period was a round 33.8688 MHz / 60 or / 50 Hz. On hardware it
is lines x line length on the video clock (mednafen psx/gpu.cpp): NTSC
263 lines (262.5 per field interlaced) of 3412.5 clocks at 53.693182 MHz,
PAL 314 (312.5) of 3405 at 53.203425 MHz: NTSC 59.826 / 59.940 Hz, PAL
49.761 / 50.000 Hz. GP1(08h) bit 5 now selects the field period too.

Dancing Stage Fusion (PAL, progressive) adds 20.096 ms of song clock per
VBlank; at 50 Hz its steps ran 0.48% ahead of its music (about 0.4 s by
the end of a song). Measured after: 75.001 ticks per second of its audio
(was 75.360), no drift from first note to last. Host pacing follows the
live period.
